From 209ccf5ae300855d74ee2d9fc8622abbfd0b47df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Impre-visible <69050895+Impre-visible@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:13:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] GPU: VICTORY_TEXTURE_MIP_DROP=0..3 starts host copies of
 placed textures that many levels down (off by default)

Port of ztrx PR #84 (antikohza, after Marvisak/VIctory#2146; in fork/z2 as
082f8b19 / merge cb0ac38) onto cool_fox's held levels instead of its own
subresource remapping: a placed 2D texture the title fills, of at least
VICTORY_TEXTURE_MIP_DROP_MIN_SIZE (1024) on both sides, gets its host copy
from level min(drop, levels - 2) on (resource::base_level), so views below
that level show it (descriptor::host::from_base), uploads read from it, and
a view of a larger level never makes the copy grow past it (want_level).
Such a texture is not made level by level (VICTORY_LEVELS_ON_DEMAND); with
the held levels on (LEVELS_ON_DEMAND unset) the copy starts at the larger
of the dropped level and the first level viewed. The held-levels line is
logged when the drop is on and names its value.

No automatic drop by VRAM size (fork/z2 enables 1 on <= 8 GB cards).

